><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3594\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3557\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3520\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-0.2\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3974\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3936\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3897\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-0.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4364\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4325\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4286\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" 13194139534445 17592186045417 true] [17592186421851 1072 #uuid "8cf1eb9f-850d-5920-b6a9-b29ec6415a62" 13194139534445 17592186045417 true] [17592186421851 1074 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a normal population, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ has the distribution\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(11,\\frac{{12}^{2}}{72}) \\\\  & ∼N(11,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're required to find $P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3).$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3) & =P(\\frac{10.75-11}{\\sqrt{2}}<Z<\\frac{11.3-11}{\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =P(-0.18<Z<0.21) \\\\  & =Φ(0.21)-Φ(-0.18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.21)=0.5832, \\\\ Φ(-0.18)=0.4286.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3) & =Φ(0.21)-Φ(-0.18) \\\\  & =0.5832-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.1546.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534445 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-211e8525-9c7c-5f08-90b9-8bafbce89824" 17592186421831 "answer-3aa5c52e-8e77-5a89-a2be-c5d48e02d707" 17592186421832 "answer-3d1645e2-c686-52f4-a67a-bc7ecd06